# Copy to .env.local and adjust.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables are inlined into the client bundle at build time and
# are therefore public. Never put a secret behind that prefix.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT LIVES HERE AND WHAT DOES NOT
#
# Only variables this app actually reads. The server-side secrets --
# MONGO_URI, KAVENEGAR_API_KEY, KAVENEGAR_SENDER, CLOUDINARY_* -- belong in
# apps/api/.env and are deliberately NOT duplicated here. This app never talks
# to Mongo, never sends an SMS and never uploads a file; it reaches all of that
# through the API. Listing a gateway key in a Next env file is also how one
# eventually acquires a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and ships to the browser.
#
#   Variable                  Where it goes
#   ------------------------  -------------------------------
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL       here
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL      here
#   JWT_SECRET                here AND apps/api/.env, identical
#   MONGO_URI                 apps/api/.env
#   ALLOWED_ORIGIN            apps/api/.env
#   APP_BASE_URL              apps/api/.env (the API's name for this app's
#                             origin -- same value as NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL)
#   SMS_PROVIDER, KAVENEGAR_* apps/api/.env
#   CLOUDINARY_*              apps/api/.env
#
# GOING TO PRODUCTION
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL  is baked in at BUILD time, not read at boot. Changing
#                        it means a rebuild and redeploy -- setting it only in
#                        the runtime environment leaves the old value in the
#                        bundle. On Vercel, set it as a Project Environment
#                        Variable before the build, not after.
#   JWT_SECRET           must match apps/api/.env exactly, or the middleware
#                        rejects every session the API issues and users bounce
#                        back to the login page in a loop.
#
# DEPLOY.md walks through the rest.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the Express API, including the /api/v1 suffix.
#
# THIS IS FETCHED BY THE BROWSER, so it must be an origin the browser can
# reach -- never a Docker service name like http://api:4100, which resolves
# only inside the compose network.
#
#   local dev        http://localhost:4100/api/v1
#   docker compose   http://localhost:4100/api/v1   (set as a build arg)
#   production       https://g-dash-api.onrender.com/api/v1
#
# There is NO fallback in the code (src/lib/api.ts throws when it is unset),
# because one variable serves all three environments and a default would be
# wrong in two of them -- silently, by compiling localhost into the bundle
# every visitor downloads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4100/api/v1

# Public origin of this app, used for absolute URLs in metadata. The API knows
# the same value as APP_BASE_URL.
#   Vercel -> https://g-dash.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# MUST be byte-identical to JWT_SECRET in apps/api/.env.
#
# src/middleware.ts verifies the API's session cookie locally rather than
# calling /me on every navigation, which means this app needs the same signing
# key. Deliberately NOT prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ -- it is read only in
# middleware, at run time, and never reaches the browser bundle.
#
# NOTE FOR SPLIT DEPLOYMENTS: on separate registrable domains the middleware
# cannot see the API's cookie at all, so this secret stops being enough on its
# own. See the cookie note under ALLOWED_ORIGIN in apps/api/.env.example.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string-at-least-32-chars
